    "/api/auth/status": {
      "delete": {
        "operationId": "delete_api_auth_status",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "successful response"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Auth Status",
        "tags": [
          "Authentication"
        ]
      },
      "get": {
        "description": "`{needsSetup, authenticated, email, defaultAuth, source, isAdmin}` — **default mode: the dashboard ships OPEN with a seeded default admin (`admin@jimesh.local` / `admin`)**; `needsSetup:false, authenticated:true, defaultAuth:true`. Personalizing via change-password/change-email flips `defaultAuth:false` and the real session gate engages. TASK-025: `source` distinguishes the login paths honestly — `\"keycloak\"` sessions additionally carry `user: {sub, email, displayName}` from the provisioned `users` row; `\"password\"` sessions are the single operator and have **no** user row (`user` field absent). SPRINT-138: `isAdmin` is the backend's OWN OPA decision (`policy.IsAdminXWorkspaceScope` — password operator or Keycloak `jimesh-admin` realm role), the gate for the dashboard's admin-only workspace switcher; `false` when unauthenticated, fail-closed `false` when the policy engine did not load",
        "operationId": "get_api_auth_status",
        "responses": {
